NOTE Agenda item 2: Why we're doing this, goals and success measures

40
00:06:52.059 --> 00:07:00.513
<v Priya Nair>Daniel, can you set the scene? Why are we doing this, and what does success look like?</v>

41
00:07:05.059 --> 00:07:15.186
<v Daniel Brooks>Yeah. So today, online orders are about 8 percent of our sales, and almost all of that comes through the website.</v>

42
00:07:15.593 --> 00:07:28.554
<v Daniel Brooks>And the website on a phone is, let's be honest, painful. Every one of our competitors has an app, and we keep losing younger families to them.</v>

43
00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:41.595
<v Daniel Brooks>So the first goal is growth. I want to grow online orders from 8 percent to 20 percent of our sales within twelve months of launch.</v>

44
00:07:41.846 --> 00:07:55.004
<v Daniel Brooks>Second is checkout. On the mobile website it takes people about four minutes to check out. In the app I want checkout to take under a minute.</v>

45
00:07:55.321 --> 00:08:07.537
<v Daniel Brooks>And third is reputation. I want a rating of at least 4.5 stars in both app stores. We don't get a second chance with reviews.</v>

46
00:08:07.812 --> 00:08:13.271
<v Daniel Brooks>If we launch at three stars, we stay at three stars.</v>

47
00:08:17.167 --> 00:08:18.903
<v Priya Nair>So, three objectives.</v>

48
00:08:19.302 --> 00:08:31.946
<v Priya Nair>Grow online orders to 20 percent of sales within a year of launch, checkout in under a minute, and a rating of 4.5 stars or better.</v>

49
00:08:35.958 --> 00:08:37.836
<v Daniel Brooks>That's it.</v>

50
00:08:42.509 --> 00:08:56.106
<v Tom Wallace>Can I add one from the quality side? I'd like a target of 99.5 percent crash-free sessions. If we're aiming for 4.5 stars, crashes are what kill that.</v>

51
00:09:00.088 --> 00:09:02.009
<v Daniel Brooks>Agreed. Add it.</v>

52
00:09:06.572 --> 00:09:18.401
<v Marcus Chen>And performance. The app needs to load in under two seconds on 4G. Otherwise people give up before they even see the home screen.</v>

53
00:09:22.425 --> 00:09:30.427
<v Hannah Lee>Can we also say "on a mid-range Android phone"? Everything is fast on the latest iPhone.</v>

54
00:09:34.973 --> 00:09:41.071
<v Marcus Chen>Good point. Under two seconds on 4G, on a mid-range Android phone.</v>

55
00:09:45.057 --> 00:09:55.410
<v Priya Nair>Okay, I've got both. Loads in under two seconds on 4G on a mid-range Android phone, and 99.5 percent crash-free sessions.</v>

56
00:09:55.565 --> 00:10:08.528
<v Priya Nair>Hannah, before we go into scope, can you share what came out of the customer workshops? I think it explains a lot of what's on the list.</v>

57
00:10:12.901 --> 00:10:23.381
<v Hannah Lee>Sure. We ran four workshops in November with about forty customers, mostly parents and people who already shop with us online.</v>

58
00:10:23.657 --> 00:10:27.407
<v Hannah Lee>Three things came up again and again.</v>

59
00:10:27.852 --> 00:10:40.703
<v Hannah Lee>The first one is time. People do their grocery order in small gaps, waiting at school pickup, on the bus, in the ten minutes before bed.</v>

60
00:10:41.078 --> 00:10:46.495
<v Hannah Lee>So anything that takes more than a few taps loses them.</v>

61
00:10:46.725 --> 00:10:56.705
<v Hannah Lee>The second is substitutions. People hate opening the door and finding oat milk instead of regular milk with no warning.</v>

62
00:10:57.037 --> 00:11:03.539
<v Hannah Lee>Several of them said it was the main reason they stopped ordering online.</v>

63
00:11:03.803 --> 00:11:07.871
<v Hannah Lee>And the third is "where is my order".</v>

64
00:11:08.113 --> 00:11:22.102
<v Hannah Lee>When the delivery window is two hours long, people want to see when the driver is actually coming, so they don't have to stay home for the whole window.</v>

65
00:11:26.606 --> 00:11:35.950
<v Daniel Brooks>That matches what customer service tells me. "Where is my order" is the number one reason people call us.</v>

66
00:11:40.311 --> 00:11:50.089
<v Priya Nair>That's really useful, because those three things map directly onto checkout, substitutions and tracking. Okay, let's go through the list.</v>

